<Base title="About"><article class="prose"><div class="meta">About the journal</div><h1>A voice beneath the folds.</h1><p class="meta">Safaa wa Noor</p><aside class="notice">Temporary biography — to be reviewed and personalised before publication.</aside><p>I am an Algerian Muslim woman writing at the intersection of faith, heritage, technology, and modern life.</p><p>Under the Haik is an independent journal about the questions that stay with us: how we live our faith, what we inherit, and how we find our way in a changing world.</p><p>Here, Algerian and Amazigh heritage sit alongside reflections on Muslim womanhood, North African history, society, motherhood, and digital culture. These subjects are connected by a desire to look closely and write thoughtfully.</p><h2>A note on religious writing</h2><p>Articles about religion are personal reflections and research. They are not fatwas or substitutes for guidance from qualified scholars. Sources and the limits of a personal perspective matter here.</p></article></Base>
